BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairlocal": "https://montclairlocal.news/event/jump-start-back-to-school-learning-with-bank-of-america-museums-on-us/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairlocal
X-SOURCE:Montclair Local News
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260906T170000
DTSTAMP:20260901T160544Z
CREATED:20260901T160544Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T160544Z
UID:10141304-1788595200-1788714000@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:Jump-Start Back-to-school Learning With Bank Of America Museums On Us
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Private Bank cardholders can receive FREE general admission to cultural attractions across New York City and New Jersey on Saturday and Sunday. \nWHEN: Saturday\, September 5th & Sunday\, September 6th (+ the first full weekend of each month) \nWHERE: Learn something new this month with a visit to a participating cultural institution\, including:\nCooper Hewitt\, Smithsonian Design Museum\, 2 East 91st Street\, New York\, NY 10128\nThe Intrepid Museum\, Pier 86 W 46th\, New York\, NY 10036\nThe Jewish Museum\, 1109 5th Ave\, New York\, NY 10128 (Sundays only)\nThe Metropolitan Museum of Art – The Met Cloisters\, 99 Margaret Corbin Dr\, New York\, NY 10040\nThe Metropolitan Museum of Art – The Met Fifth Avenue\, 1000 5th Ave\, New York\, NY 10028\nHunterdon Art Museum\, 7 Lower Center Street\, Clinton\, NJ 08809\nLiberty Science Center\, 222 Jersey City Boulevard\, Jersey City\, NJ 07305\nMontclair Art Museum\, 3 South Mountain Ave.\, Montclair\, NJ 07042\nMorris Museum\, 6 Normandy Heights Road\, Morristown\, NJ 07960\nThe Newark Museum of Art\, 49 Washington Street\, Newark\, NJ 07102\nNew York Botanical Garden\, 2900 Southern Blvd.\, Bronx\, NY 10458 \nWHY: Bank of America believes the arts have a unique ability to connect people and communities and help local economies thrive. Through Museums on Us\, Bank of America provides its cardholders with free access during the first full weekend of every month to artistic and cultural experiences in New Jersey at celebrated institutions ranging from art\, children’s and history museums to botanical gardens\, and science centers. This is one example of how the bank strengthens the local communities it serves in\, creates greater cultural understanding\, and expands accessibility to the arts. \nHOW: Use the bank’s location finder tool to search for participating cultural attractions. Please check with our partners directly for current operating hours and admission guidelines. Present your Bank of America\, Merrill or Bank of America Private Bank credit or debit card along with a photo ID to gain free general admission to any participating institution during the first full weekend (Saturday and Sunday) of each month. Cardholders only; guests are not eligible for free admission. Program excludes fundraising events\, special exhibitions\, and ticketed shows. Not to be combined with other offers. Museum participation varies. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/jump-start-back-to-school-learning-with-bank-of-america-museums-on-us/
LOCATION:Multiple locations in New Jersey and NYC
CATEGORIES:Kids & Families
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Bank-of-America-Emblem-scaled.png
END:VEVENT
